        "id": 20469,
        "name": "frankfrank",
        "username": "frankfrank",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5daacb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-12-26T15:13:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We ran into this question last night: We had <em>Shroud of Silent Mist</em> is in play, who had damaged towns in its lands. Then the blight card flipped and turned out to be <em>All Things Weaken</em>. Among other things, the card says \"Starting next turn, invaders have -1 health\".</p>\n<p>In this case, what happens to towns which are already damaged and don't heal until next turn? Do they keep 1 health point, or would they be destroyed immediately as soon as the next turn starts? And what would happen to a city that has taken 1 damage before the blight card flipped?</p>\n<p>Many thanks,</p>\n<p>Frank</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:34.985Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 252,
        "reads": 5,
        "readers_count": 4,
        "score": 1261.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 20466,
        "topic_slug": "how-does-all-things-weaken-interact-with-shroud-of-silent-mist",
        "display_username": "frankfrank",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
